========== Identifiability ridge ==========
     method crate   ptran    beta      R0 ridge_ratio_crate ridge_ratio_ptran
        ABC 69.90  366.93  16.454  16.454           4.24798            22.301
    ABC-SMC 61.26  164.63   2.418   2.418          25.33431            68.085
 NelderMead 14.14 1168.37 978.528 978.528           0.01445             1.194
         DE 35.66   74.96   1.561   1.561          22.85021            48.035
     BiLSTM    NA      NA   2.858   2.421                NA                NA

ridge_ratio = median APE of the factor divided by median APE of beta.
Values >> 1 mean the method recovers the PRODUCT far better than the
FACTORS -- the expected signature of a non-identifiable direction.
A ratio near 1 for a point estimator is more suspicious than reassuring:
it usually means the objective happened to break the tie arbitrarily.

